  "post_fetch_notes": [
    "Do not apply both patch_noetic.py and the equivalent recorded patches: they duplicate the same changes.",
    "VIO sparse-feature compatibility guards were applied only to UROS; AMOV VIO source is its pristine recorded Git commit.",
    "For the VIO underlay, create CATKIN_IGNORE in standalone DBoW2 and opengv; opengv_catkin and dbow2_catkin build them externally.",
    "Dense minkindr patch reproduces the ignored optional Python package; the empty-file Git patch preserves the deployed empty CATKIN_IGNORE.",
    "PGMO is a modern API compatibility port; it is not the original Kimera-Multi v1.0.0 package combination.",
    "Build OpenGV guard independently for each architecture. Generate a new runtime_gate.sha256 from the tested local shared library, never reuse the other architecture checksum.",
    "The rejected nearest-depth-query VIO candidate is deliberately absent."
  ]
